<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23230" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαιμόνιον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>divine Power, Divinity,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.87
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				894
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				1.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				382e
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δαιμόνιον ἄρ᾽ ἢ θεὸς ἢ θεοῦ
					ἔργον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1398a15
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1419a9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ θεοὶ εἴσονται καὶ τὸ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					19.239
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοβεῖσθαι μή τι δ. πράγματ᾽
				ἐλαύνῃ</span> some <i>fatality,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				9.54
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ τοῦ δ.</span> the favours of
				<i>forlune,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Epin.</u>
				992d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>inferior divine being,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταξὺ θεοῦ τε καὶ θνητοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					202e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καινὰ δ. εἰσφέρειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					1.1.2
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				24c
			</span></i>, cf. Vett. Val.<i><span class="en">
				67.5
			</span></i>, etc.; applied to the <i>'genius'</i> of Socrates, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				1.1.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				40a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tht.</u>
				151a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Euthphr.</u>
				3b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>evil spirit,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. φαῦλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chrysipp.Stoic.
					2.338
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>De.</u>
				32.17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>To.</u>
				3.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				7.22
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Lond.</u>
				1.46.120
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A. D.)</span>.</div>
